<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26087" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάτονος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διατείνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>on the stretch, vehement,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὖραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>CP</u>
					2.3.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>extending from front to back,</i> of <i>bonding courses</i>
			in a wall, <i><span class="en">
				Vitr.
				2.8.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in Music,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάτονον</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γένος</span>), τό,
				<i>the diatonic scale,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρωματικόν, ἐναρμόνιον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aristox.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				p.19M.
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. μέλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					1.18
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. μελῳδία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Comp.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
